Z||000008||84Bill||05-18-2001||11:38 AM||||HEHEHE do a photo search for "Fiero" what bone heads! Not only do they have it as a ZM4 but also an SM4. Jeaz man does it ever end? the pain. the PAIN!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mr.Frosty||05-18-2001||11:54 AM||||Pontiaddict,I was bieng sarcastic.Pontiac is a division of GM.Specifically it was Chevrolet who disliked the Fiero.It was starting to take the glory away from the Vette.Especially the '89 '90 models.I do think that Pontiac should have had the power in determining whether it stayed or went.If it did,then they failed us and it.The press was largely to blame for the reputation of the car's image.I have heard that they did a lot to keep it alive to that point "88",but I'll take that with a grain of salt.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top-Sold <BR>85 GT Turbo-project car||||reg||1
